{"id":"01999bad-64da-4224-8834-00501b6b48fa","object":"chat.completion","created":1784999362,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    names = [seg['name'] for seg in segments]\\n    importances = [seg['importance'] for seg in segments]\\n    minima = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]\\n    capacities = [seg['capacity'] for seg in segments]\\n\\n    total_min = sum(minima)\\n    total_cap = sum(capacities)\\n    if budget < total_min or budget > total_cap:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Budget not in feasible range\\\")\\n\\n    alloc = list(minima)\\n    remaining = budget - total_min\\n\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if alloc[i] < capacities[i]:\\n                score = importances[i] / (alloc[i] + 1)\\n                if score > best_score:\\n                    best_score = score\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Cannot allocate remaining budget\\\")\\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n\\n    total = sum(alloc)\\n    by_name = {names[i]: alloc[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    return {\\\"allocations\\\": alloc, \\\"by_name\\\": by_name, \\\"total\\\": total}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that processes the payload. The payload has \"segments\" (list of objects with name, importance, minimum, capacity) and \"budget\" (integer). We need to allocate budget exactly, starting with minimums, then greedily allocate remaining budget to segments based on importance divided by next allocated position (or maybe by (importance / (current_allocation+1)?) The description: \"While budget remains, give one token to the segment maximizing importance divided by its next allocated position.\" That 